# Copy to zot.secrets and fill in, or just run deploy.sh -- it writes
# this file with three generated passwords on a first run and never
# touches it again.
#
# zot.secrets is untracked: the repo's .gitignore excludes *.secrets,
# the same rule that keeps ../grafana/grafana-api.secrets out. It is
# sourced by deploy.sh, so it is shell, and the values must be quoted
# if they contain anything the shell would look at.
#
# Changing a password here and re-running deploy.sh rewrites
# /etc/zot/htpasswd. zot watches that file and reloads it in place,
# so no restart is needed and no push in flight is interrupted.
#
# The three accounts exist because /etc/zot/config.json names them:
#
#   admin    Full rights, including delete. The account you log into
#            the web UI with. Nothing automated should use it.
#   ci       read + create + update on every repository: the push
#            account for builds. Cannot delete.
#   metrics  Read only, and the sole account allowed to GET /metrics.
#            This is what Prometheus on snoc-beelink authenticates
#            with -- see ../prometheus/README.md.
#
# Anonymous pulls are allowed regardless of any of this, so nodes that
# only consume images need no credentials at all.

ZOT_ADMIN_PASSWORD=""
ZOT_CI_PASSWORD=""
ZOT_METRICS_PASSWORD=""
